1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,619
The flag on the Puri temple flies against the wind,

2
00:00:03,619 --> 00:00:06,514
or so people say. The wind comes from the sea,

3
00:00:06,514 --> 00:00:09,410
and still the flag flutters toward the sea.

4
00:00:09,410 --> 00:00:12,667
For centuries, pilgrims have folded their hands at this sight.

5
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:17,010
And today, even weather scientists watch this flag closely.

6
00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:18,893
This is not the only mystery.

7
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:22,282
They say the temple's shadow is never seen on the ground.

8
00:00:22,282 --> 00:00:26,048
The wheel on top of the spire seems to look straight at you from every direction.

9
00:00:26,048 --> 00:00:29,438
In the kitchen, the topmost pot cooks first.

10
00:00:29,438 --> 00:00:33,580
The moment you cross the Singhadwara, the sound of the sea goes silent.

11
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:37,543
In this video, for every mystery, you will get both sides.

12
00:00:37,543 --> 00:00:41,507
On one side, the devotee's faith; on the other, the calculations of science.

13
00:00:41,507 --> 00:00:45,470
We will not call anyone wrong. We will only lay out the evidence,

14
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:49,830
and the decision will be yours. Come, let's go to the Odisha seashore.

15
00:00:49,830 --> 00:00:52,646
First, let's see what the scriptures say.

16
00:00:52,646 --> 00:00:55,463
There is a part of the Skanda Purana called Utkala Khanda.

17
00:00:55,463 --> 00:00:56,871
Utkala means old Odisha.

18
00:00:56,871 --> 00:01:00,743
In this part, the glory of Puri is written in detail.

19
00:01:00,743 --> 00:01:03,208
And here is one very special point,

20
00:01:03,208 --> 00:01:05,320
which is the foundation of the whole story.

21
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:08,899
The Skanda Purana calls Puri Purushottama Kshetra.

22
00:01:08,899 --> 00:01:12,032
Kshetra means a sacred land, a place of pilgrimage.

23
00:01:12,032 --> 00:01:15,164
According to the scripture, God is everywhere.

24
00:01:15,164 --> 00:01:18,296
Still, this kshetra is the greatest of all.

25
00:01:18,296 --> 00:01:22,770
Because this place has itself become the body of the Supreme Lord.

26
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:24,877
Just feel this for a moment.

27
00:01:24,877 --> 00:01:28,390
For the scripture, Puri is not just a city with a temple.

28
00:01:28,390 --> 00:01:30,498
The sand here, the seashore,

29
00:01:30,498 --> 00:01:32,956
all of it is part of that divine form.

30
00:01:32,956 --> 00:01:36,820
That is why pilgrims here touch the ground and press it to their foreheads.

31
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:40,131
Now a popular story, the kind grandmothers tell.

32
00:01:40,131 --> 00:01:43,856
A king saw God in a dream.

33
00:01:43,856 --> 00:01:47,168
A divine log came floating in the sea.

34
00:01:47,168 --> 00:01:49,651
The idols were made from that very log.

35
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:53,790
This story has been passed down by word of mouth, generation after generation.

36
00:01:53,790 --> 00:01:55,283
That is why the idols of Jagannath,

37
00:01:55,283 --> 00:01:58,269
Balabhadra and Subhadra are made of wood.

38
00:01:58,269 --> 00:02:01,255
Not of stone or metal. Devotees say,

39
00:02:01,255 --> 00:02:03,868
this temple runs by its own rules.

40
00:02:03,868 --> 00:02:06,854
And this is where those mysteries begin,

41
00:02:06,854 --> 00:02:08,720
The place we're going to walk through today.

42
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:13,766
Now let's leave the scriptures behind and step into the world of measuring and checking.

43
00:02:13,766 --> 00:02:16,095
The Archaeological Survey of India, that is, ASI,

44
00:02:16,095 --> 00:02:19,200
looks after the country's old buildings.

45
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:23,081
When did ASI take this temple into its care?

46
00:02:23,081 --> 00:02:25,410
The answer is hidden in one year.

47
00:02:25,410 --> 00:02:26,653
The year was 1975.

48
00:02:26,653 --> 00:02:30,795
ASI took the Jagannath temple under national protection.

49
00:02:30,795 --> 00:02:34,938
Conservation means saving a building from falling apart and repairing it.

50
00:02:34,938 --> 00:02:38,252
This decision was made through an official notification.

51
00:02:38,252 --> 00:02:41,980
Since then, its walls have been looked after regularly.

52
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:45,777
ASI's records consider it a temple that is centuries old.

53
00:02:45,777 --> 00:02:48,308
Its structure is in the Kalinga style.

54
00:02:48,308 --> 00:02:52,105
Kalinga style means the special architecture of ancient Odisha.

55
00:02:52,105 --> 00:02:55,481
In it, the tower gets narrower as it goes up,

56
00:02:55,481 --> 00:02:57,590
like the peak of a mountain.

57
00:02:57,590 --> 00:03:01,105
This kind of tall tower is called a Rekha Deula.

58
00:03:01,105 --> 00:03:04,619
Deula means the temple's inner sanctum and its tower. It's called Rekha because

59
00:03:04,619 --> 00:03:08,134
its walls rise up in a curving line.

60
00:03:08,134 --> 00:03:12,000
This same curve will come in useful later in the mystery of the shadow.

61
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,745
And sitting at the very top of this tower is the Neela Chakra.

62
00:03:15,745 --> 00:03:19,865
It is believed to be the symbol of Lord Vishnu's Sudarshan Chakra.

63
00:03:19,865 --> 00:03:23,610
According to ASI's records, it is made of ashtadhatu.

64
00:03:23,610 --> 00:03:27,730
Ashtadhatu means an alloy made by mixing several metals.

65
00:03:27,730 --> 00:03:30,342
And its size? Around 3.5 metres.

66
00:03:30,342 --> 00:03:33,825
That is, much taller than even a tall man.

67
00:03:33,825 --> 00:03:38,179
Such a heavy metal wheel, on such a high tower. Just think,

68
00:03:38,179 --> 00:03:42,968
how was it carried up there without today's machines?

69
00:03:42,968 --> 00:03:45,580
We will raise this same question again later.

70
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:46,815
People say that

71
00:03:46,815 --> 00:03:50,518
every day a priest-servant climbs this tower.

72
00:03:50,518 --> 00:03:55,045
He takes down the old flag near the chakra and ties up a new one.

73
00:03:55,045 --> 00:03:57,515
Using only his hands and feet.

74
00:03:57,515 --> 00:04:01,630
The devotees standing below watch this sight holding their breath.

75
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:04,863
Now, the first big question that every pilgrim asks.

76
00:04:04,863 --> 00:04:07,378
Why does the flag fly against the wind?

77
00:04:07,378 --> 00:04:10,971
On this, devotees and scientists say different things.

78
00:04:10,971 --> 00:04:14,564
Listen carefully to both. First, the side of faith,

79
00:04:14,564 --> 00:04:16,360
then the calculation of weather science.

80
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:20,331
For the devotees, the answer is simple. It is the Lord's divine play.

81
00:04:20,331 --> 00:04:23,220
A flag that flies against the law of nature,

82
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:26,108
is a divine sign. Many pilgrims say,

83
00:04:26,108 --> 00:04:30,080
they have seen it with their own eyes. Standing on the sand,

84
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:33,690
sea wind on their face, and the flag flying the opposite way.

85
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:37,785
Now let's talk about the India Meteorological Department, that is, IMD.

86
00:04:37,785 --> 00:04:41,368
IMD is the country's official weather department.

87
00:04:41,368 --> 00:04:49,046
It says small local swirls of wind form along the eastern coast.

88
00:04:49,046 --> 00:04:55,700
Along with the larger weather, the sea breeze and heat together create these swirls.

89
00:04:55,700 --> 00:05:01,630
Sea breeze means the cool wind that blows from the sea toward the land during the day.

90
00:05:01,630 --> 00:05:04,594
In the evening it often reverses,

91
00:05:04,594 --> 00:05:06,712
from the land toward the sea.

92
00:05:06,712 --> 00:05:10,524
So on the coast, the wind direction keeps changing.

93
00:05:10,524 --> 00:05:13,489
The wind you feel down below,

94
00:05:13,489 --> 00:05:16,030
can be different up above.

95
00:05:16,030 --> 00:05:18,246
There is one more reason: the thermal eddy.

96
00:05:18,246 --> 00:05:22,678
A thermal eddy is a whirl of air spinning near a hot surface.

97
00:05:22,678 --> 00:05:26,002
The temple's curved spire heats up in the sun.

98
00:05:26,002 --> 00:05:28,956
Around it the air bends and spins.

99
00:05:28,956 --> 00:05:32,280
Up there, the flag flutters with this spinning air.

100
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:33,601
So scientists say,

101
00:05:33,601 --> 00:05:37,564
the flag is actually flying with the wind up above.

102
00:05:37,564 --> 00:05:40,536
It's just that this wind is opposite to the wind on the ground.

103
00:05:40,536 --> 00:05:44,168
Devotees say even this explanation is part of the same divine play.

104
00:05:44,168 --> 00:05:46,810
Both views still go side by side today.

105
00:05:46,810 --> 00:05:49,052
The next mystery, the shadow. People say,

106
00:05:49,052 --> 00:05:52,894
at no time of the day is the temple's shadow seen on the ground.

107
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:56,417
Noon or evening, the spire's shadow does not fall on the sand.

108
00:05:56,417 --> 00:05:59,619
This is on the lips of every guide in Puri.

109
00:05:59,619 --> 00:06:01,540
But is it really so?

110
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:05,188
Analysts who work on Kalinga architecture say,

111
00:06:05,188 --> 00:06:06,810
the temple does cast a shadow.

112
00:06:06,810 --> 00:06:10,864
It's just that the shadow doesn't fall where we look for it.

113
00:06:10,864 --> 00:06:14,918
The spire of the Rekha Deula gets thinner as it goes up.

114
00:06:14,918 --> 00:06:17,350
Its walls are not straight, they are curved.

115
00:06:17,350 --> 00:06:21,748
The temple stands on a wide, high base.

116
00:06:21,748 --> 00:06:27,796
This is called a podium, that is, the raised platform beneath a building.

117
00:06:27,796 --> 00:06:33,294
The spire's shadow first falls on its own tiers.

118
00:06:33,294 --> 00:06:37,142
Tiers means layers like steps on a wall.

119
00:06:37,142 --> 00:06:42,640
Then on the walls of the platform and the nearby roofs.

120
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:45,898
The temple is built aligned with each main direction.

121
00:06:45,898 --> 00:06:50,603
That is why the shadow from the sun's steep angles shrinks inward.

122
00:06:50,603 --> 00:06:53,499
In the open ground outside, no long shadow spreads out.

123
00:06:53,499 --> 00:06:57,480
So to the eye, it looks like the shadow has vanished. Analysts say,

124
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,290
it is just hidden.

125
00:06:59,290 --> 00:07:02,332
Listen to the devotees' answer too. They say,

126
00:07:02,332 --> 00:07:05,754
such precise measurement centuries ago is itself a miracle.

127
00:07:05,754 --> 00:07:10,317
Someone planned it so carefully that even the shadow stays inside the spire.

128
00:07:10,317 --> 00:07:16,020
Here science and faith seem to be saying the same thing in different words.

129
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:18,250
Now, the mystery of the Neela Chakra. They say,

130
00:07:18,250 --> 00:07:20,161
From anywhere in Puri you look,

131
00:07:20,161 --> 00:07:23,346
the wheel appears to be facing you. From the east,

132
00:07:23,346 --> 00:07:25,257
from the west, from any lane.

133
00:07:25,257 --> 00:07:28,123
As if it is looking straight at every devotee.

134
00:07:28,123 --> 00:07:30,990
Children also play this game, moving around again and again.

135
00:07:30,990 --> 00:07:34,960
ASI records tell an interesting thing.

136
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:40,418
The outer rim of the wheel is open toward every main direction.

137
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:46,869
Its structure is such that it looks almost the same from every side.

138
00:07:46,869 --> 00:07:49,846
So geometry, the mathematics of shapes,

139
00:07:49,846 --> 00:07:53,320
plays a big role in this feeling.

140
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:57,012
Still, for the devotee this is not just a metal wheel.

141
00:07:57,012 --> 00:07:59,027
A flag is tied on the Neela Chakra,

142
00:07:59,027 --> 00:08:01,712
and people bow down to it from far away.

143
00:08:01,712 --> 00:08:04,397
Many pilgrims are not able to go inside the temple.

144
00:08:04,397 --> 00:08:08,090
For them, seeing the wheel is considered the complete darshan.

145
00:08:08,090 --> 00:08:13,341
Now let's go to the temple kitchen, where the Mahaprasad is made.

146
00:08:13,341 --> 00:08:17,542
Mahaprasad means the holy food offered to God.

147
00:08:17,542 --> 00:08:23,319
Here clay pots are stacked one on top of another and cooked

148
00:08:23,319 --> 00:08:26,469
on a wood fire.

149
00:08:26,469 --> 00:08:29,620
And here is one more mystery.

150
00:08:29,620 --> 00:08:31,667
The kitchen workers say,

151
00:08:31,667 --> 00:08:34,941
the topmost pot cooks first.

152
00:08:34,941 --> 00:08:38,625
While the fire is at the very bottom. Seems backwards, doesn't it?

153
00:08:38,625 --> 00:08:43,537
The Centre for Culinary Heritage Documentation has recorded a debate on this.

154
00:08:43,537 --> 00:08:47,630
On one side, the cook's experience; on the other, questions of physics.

155
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:50,358
Physicists say, this is the work of convection.

156
00:08:50,358 --> 00:08:54,451
Convection means hot steam rising and carrying the heat along with it.

157
00:08:54,451 --> 00:08:56,497
Clay pots are porous,

158
00:08:56,497 --> 00:08:58,543
meaning they have tiny holes in them.

159
00:08:58,543 --> 00:09:00,931
The steam rises up through these holes,

160
00:09:00,931 --> 00:09:04,000
and the whole stack becomes like a furnace.

161
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,127
How the heat in this furnace reaches its level,

162
00:09:07,127 --> 00:09:09,212
is still being debated.

163
00:09:09,212 --> 00:09:12,339
The cooks stand firm on what they say. Scientists say,

164
00:09:12,339 --> 00:09:14,771
without measurement, it is hard to say for sure.

165
00:09:14,771 --> 00:09:17,898
And the sound of the sea going silent at Singhadwara?

166
00:09:17,898 --> 00:09:20,330
There is no measurement of that in front of us yet.

167
00:09:20,330 --> 00:09:24,091
Now, the things that nobody knows even today.

168
00:09:24,091 --> 00:09:28,270
How was such a heavy wheel lifted to such a high peak?

169
00:09:28,270 --> 00:09:32,867
There is no complete record of that medieval engineering method.

170
00:09:32,867 --> 00:09:36,210
No plan, no written calculation.

171
00:09:36,210 --> 00:09:38,300
This question is still open.

172
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:41,576
And one more open question: the air above the peak.

173
00:09:41,576 --> 00:09:43,397
How the air moves up there,

174
00:09:43,397 --> 00:09:46,309
a full scientific model of that has not been built yet.

175
00:09:46,309 --> 00:09:49,585
A model means a computer calculation of how the air moves.

176
00:09:49,585 --> 00:09:53,590
Until that is built, the whole story of the flag is incomplete.

177
00:09:53,590 --> 00:09:56,946
If you go to Puri today, what can you see?

178
00:09:56,946 --> 00:10:00,303
Stand on the seashore and look at the direction of the flag.

179
00:10:00,303 --> 00:10:02,540
Then feel the wind on your face.

180
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:04,778
At noon, look for the shadow of the temple.

181
00:10:04,778 --> 00:10:08,880
And look at the Neela Chakra from different lanes, judge for yourself.

182
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:12,968
The temple's strong stone walls still stand today.

183
00:10:12,968 --> 00:10:16,239
The ASI has been looking after them since 1975.

184
00:10:16,239 --> 00:10:19,918
As you walk toward Singhadwara, listen to the sound of the sea.

185
00:10:19,918 --> 00:10:23,597
Decide for yourself what you feel.

186
00:10:23,597 --> 00:10:26,050
The evidence will be in front of you, the decision is yours.

187
00:10:26,050 --> 00:10:29,929
So which mystery attracts you the most? The upside-down flag,

188
00:10:29,929 --> 00:10:32,645
the hidden shadow, or the wheel that looks at you from every side?

189
00:10:32,645 --> 00:10:34,973
Write just one word in the comments.

190
00:10:34,973 --> 00:10:37,301
And if you have been to Puri,

191
00:10:37,301 --> 00:10:41,180
do tell us what you saw with your own eyes.

192
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:45,106
Next time we go to the seashore of Gujarat, Dwarka.

193
00:10:45,106 --> 00:10:49,904
They say a whole city sank into the water there. The divers,

194
00:10:49,904 --> 00:10:52,957
what did they find there?

195
00:10:52,957 --> 00:10:57,319
And what do scientists say about it? With evidence,

196
00:10:57,319 --> 00:10:59,500
we'll meet in the next story.
